diff --git a/docs/harness/log.md b/docs/harness/log.md
index 3a313eb37..05047ec89 100644
--- a/docs/harness/log.md
+++ b/docs/harness/log.md
@@ -105,3 +105,11 @@ Risks seen before the harness:
 - full-gate: Not in any gate: tools/test-integration.py and the other Python tools (they need a running server), and tests on MySQL, PostgreSQL or SQL Server (unit tests use H2 or memory only). Recorded in docs/harness/log.md.
 - local-env: debug.xml points web.path to ./traccar-web/simple, and the server stops at startup when that folder is missing (the submodule is empty in this checkout). make dev works around it with an API-only run (CONFIG_USE_ENVIRONMENT_VARIABLES=true, WEB_PATH=./target/web). The web UI cannot be served locally until the submodule question is answered.
 - fast-gate: This machine has only JDK 17 (default) and Homebrew JDK 25. The gates were verified on JDK 25 through tools/harness/java-home.sh. CI uses Temurin 21. Every Gradle run also needs Maven Central, because build.gradle resolves versions at configuration time.
+
+## 2026-11-02: position filters configurable per device
+
+Fifteen filter settings (invalid, zero, duplicate, outdated, future, past, accuracy, approximate, static, distance, max speed, min period, daily limit, daily limit interval, skip limit) are now device keys in `config/Keys.java`. The `FilterHandler` resolves each one for the position's device with `AttributeUtil.lookup`: device attribute, then groups, then server config, then the key default. The handler constructor is now `FilterHandler(cacheManager, statisticsManager)`.
+
+What I learned: the keys had `null` defaults, so they now have explicit defaults (false, 0 or 0L) to avoid unboxing errors. `filter.future` keeps its default of 86400 seconds, so a position far in the future is filtered when nothing is set; a device or group value of 0 disables it. `filter.globalDailyLimit` stays server-only.
+
+Left: no test covers the daily limit, min period, distance or max speed settings per device; they use the same lookup, but only the invalid, zero, future and group cases are tested.
